IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A, LAYER 1, second module: s 386AD (state of mind of a corporation, an unincorporated association
-- or a partnership, in a proceeding for an offence under the Part) and s 386AE (the meaning of "legal privilege").
--
-- s 386AD is a rule that other rules call: it says what counts as EVIDENCE of a body's state of mind in a prosecution under the Part
-- (the offences of ss 386AF to 386AM). It decides nothing about guilt by itself.
-- s 386AE is the test that s 386AG(6) uses to excuse an addressee from giving information.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING mean what the header of sgn-application.l4 says.

§ `Section 386AD: state of mind of a corporation, an unincorporated association or a partnership`

-- Who engaged in the conduct. For a corporation (subsection (1)) an officer, employee or agent counts; for an unincorporated association or a
-- partnership (subsection (2)) only an employee or agent counts: the text does not name an officer there.
DECLARE `s 386AD kind of person who engaged in the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AD an officer of the body`
    `s 386AD an employee of the body`
    `s 386AD an agent of the body`
    `s 386AD some other person`

-- src:25535 | 386AD.—(1) Where, in a proceeding for an offence under this Part,
-- src:25536 | it is necessary to prove the state of mind of a corporation in relation to
-- src:25537 | a particular conduct, evidence that —
-- src:25539 | (a) an officer, employee or agent of the corporation engaged in
-- src:25540 | that conduct within the scope of the officer’s, employee’s
-- src:25541 | or agent’s actual or apparent authority; and
-- src:25543 | (b) the officer, employee or agent had that state of mind,
-- src:25545 | is evidence that the corporation had that state of mind.
@ref s 386AD(1) (src:25535-25545)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the corporation in relation to a particular conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 386AD kind of person who engaged in the conduct`
      `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had that state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AD(1) the evidence is evidence that the corporation had that state of mind` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` AND `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the corporation in relation to a particular conduct`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in a proceeding for an offence under this Part, it is necessary to prove the state of mind of a corporation in relation to a particular conduct, evidence that ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-AD1 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF    (CONSIDER kind
                 WHEN `s 386AD an officer of the body` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 386AD an employee of the body` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 386AD an agent of the body` THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            AND `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority`
            AND `the person had that state of mind`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says that evidence of (a) and (b) "is evidence that the corporation had that state of mind"; it does not say that other evidence is no evidence (fork line F-AD2)

-- src:25549 | (2) Where, in a proceeding for an offence under this Part, it is
-- src:25550 | necessary to prove the state of mind of an unincorporated association
-- src:25551 | or a partnership in relation to a particular conduct, evidence that —
-- src:25553 | (a) an employee or agent of the unincorporated association or
-- src:25554 | the partnership engaged in that conduct within the scope of
-- src:25555 | the employee’s or agent’s actual or apparent authority; and
-- src:25557 | (b) the employee or agent had that state of mind,
-- src:25559 | is evidence that the unincorporated association or partnership had that
-- src:25560 | state of mind.
@ref s 386AD(2) (src:25549-25560)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the unincorporated association or partnership in relation to a particular conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 386AD kind of person who engaged in the conduct`
      `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had that state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AD(2) the evidence is evidence that the unincorporated association or partnership had that state of mind` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceeding is a proceeding for an offence under Part 11A` AND `it is necessary to prove the state of mind of the unincorporated association or partnership in relation to a particular conduct`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in a proceeding for an offence under this Part, it is necessary to prove the state of mind of an unincorporated association or a partnership in relation to a particular conduct, evidence that ..." (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-AD1 in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF    (CONSIDER kind
                 WHEN `s 386AD an employee of the body` THEN TRUE
                 WHEN `s 386AD an agent of the body` THEN TRUE
                 OTHERWISE FALSE)
            AND `the person engaged in that conduct within the scope of the person's actual or apparent authority`
            AND `the person had that state of mind`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) names "an employee or agent" only; an officer who is neither is not within it, and the subsection does not say that other evidence is no evidence (fork line F-AD2 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 386AE(1): information or a document is subject to legal privilege`

-- The five kinds of thing paragraphs (a) to (e) describe. The second "(c)" in the printed text (line 25598) is the closing words of
-- paragraph (c), not a second paragraph (finding 5 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 386AE(1) kind of information or document` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AE(1)(a) a communication between a lawyer and a client, or between a legal counsel acting as such and the legal counsel's employer`
    `s 386AE(1)(b) a communication between 2 or more lawyers acting for a client, or between 2 or more legal counsel acting as such for their employer`
    `s 386AE(1)(c) a communication between a client (or the employer of a legal counsel) and another person, between a lawyer acting for a client and the client or another person, or between a legal counsel acting as such and the employer or another person`
    `s 386AE(1)(d) an item or document enclosed with or mentioned in a communication in paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 386AE(1)(e) an item or document enclosed with or mentioned in a communication in paragraph (c)`
    `s 386AE(1) none of those kinds`

-- src:25566 | 386AE.—(1) For the purposes of this Part, information or a
-- src:25567 | document is subject to legal privilege if —
-- src:25569 | (a) it is a communication made between a lawyer and a client,
-- src:25570 | or a legal counsel acting as such and the legal counsel’s
-- src:25571 | employer, in connection with the lawyer giving legal
-- src:25576 | advice to the client or the legal counsel giving legal advice
-- src:25577 | to the employer, as the case may be;
-- src:25579 | (b) it is a communication made between 2 or more lawyers
-- src:25580 | acting for a client, or 2 or more legal counsel acting as such
-- src:25581 | for their employer, in connection with one or more of the
-- src:25582 | lawyers giving legal advice to the client or one or more of
-- src:25583 | the legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer, as the
-- src:25584 | case may be;
-- src:25586 | (c) it is a communication made —
-- src:25588 | (i) between a client, or an employer of a legal counsel,
-- src:25589 | and another person;
-- src:25591 | (ii) between a lawyer acting for a client and either the
-- src:25592 | client or another person; or
-- src:25594 | (iii) between a legal counsel acting as such for the legal
-- src:25595 | counsel’s employer and either the employer or
-- src:25596 | another person,
-- src:25598 | (c) in connection with, and for the purposes of, any legal
-- src:25599 | proceedings (including anticipated or pending legal
-- src:25600 | proceedings) in which the client or employer (as the case
-- src:25601 | may be) is or may be, or was or might have been, a party;
-- src:25603 | (d) it is an item, or a document (including its contents), that is
-- src:25604 | enclosed with or mentioned in any communication in
-- src:25605 | paragraph (a) or (b) and that is made or prepared by any
-- src:25606 | person in connection with a lawyer or legal counsel, or one
-- src:25607 | or more of the lawyers or legal counsel, in either
-- src:25608 | paragraph giving legal advice to the client or the
-- src:25609 | employer of the legal counsel, as the case may be; or
-- src:25611 | (e) it is an item, or a document (including its contents), that is
-- src:25612 | enclosed with or mentioned in any communication in
-- src:25613 | paragraph (c) and that is made or prepared by any person in
-- src:25614 | connection with, and for the purposes of, any legal
-- src:25615 | proceedings (including anticipated or pending legal
-- src:25616 | proceedings) in which the client or the employer of the
-- src:25617 | legal counsel (as the case may be) is or may be, or was or
-- src:25618 | might have been, a party,
-- src:25623 | but it is not any such communication, item or document that is made,
-- src:25624 | prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose.
@ref s 386AE(1) (src:25566-25624)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 386AE(1) kind of information or document`
      `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AE(1) the information or document is subject to legal privilege` MEANS
    IF    `it is made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but it is not any such communication, item or document that is made, prepared or held with the intention of furthering a criminal purpose"
    ELSE (IF (CONSIDER kind
              WHEN `s 386AE(1)(a) a communication between a lawyer and a client, or between a legal counsel acting as such and the legal counsel's employer` THEN `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer`
              WHEN `s 386AE(1)(b) a communication between 2 or more lawyers acting for a client, or between 2 or more legal counsel acting as such for their employer` THEN `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer`
              WHEN `s 386AE(1)(c) a communication between a client (or the employer of a legal counsel) and another person, between a lawyer acting for a client and the client or another person, or between a legal counsel acting as such and the employer or another person` THEN `it is made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party`
              WHEN `s 386AE(1)(d) an item or document enclosed with or mentioned in a communication in paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN `it is made in connection with a lawyer giving legal advice to the client, or a legal counsel giving legal advice to the employer`
              WHEN `s 386AE(1)(e) an item or document enclosed with or mentioned in a communication in paragraph (c)` THEN `it is made in connection with, and for the purposes of, legal proceedings (including anticipated or pending proceedings) in which the client or employer is or may be, or was or might have been, a party`
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information or a document is subject to legal privilege if — (a) ... (e) ..." (a failed "if", counted as the text's no, clause by clause: marginal reading (a) in NOTES.md, fork line F-AE1)

§ `Section 386AE(2): "client", "employer", "lawyer" and "legal counsel"`

-- "client" includes an agent of, or other person representing, a client and, if a client has died, a personal representative: an open list.
-- src:25628 | (2) In subsection (1) —
-- src:25630 | “client”, in relation to a lawyer, includes an agent of or other
-- src:25631 | person representing a client and, if a client has died, a
-- src:25632 | personal representative of the client;
@ref s 386AE(2) "client" (src:25628-25632)
GIVEN `the person is an agent of or other person representing a client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a personal representative of a client who has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AE(2) "client" the person is within the word client` MEANS
    IF `the person is an agent of or other person representing a client` OR `the person is a personal representative of a client who has died`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“client”, in relation to a lawyer, includes an agent of or other person representing a client and, if a client has died, a personal representative of the client" leaves the list open

-- "employer", in relation to a legal counsel, includes (a) a related corporation under s 6, (b) another public agency, (c) an employee or officer of the employer: an open list.
-- src:25634 | “employer”, in relation to a legal counsel, includes —
-- src:25636 | (a) if the employer is one of a number of corporations
-- src:25637 | that are related to each other under section 6, every
-- src:25638 | corporation so related as if the legal counsel is also
-- src:25639 | employed by each of the related corporations;
-- src:25641 | (b) if the employer is a public agency within the meaning
-- src:25642 | of section 128A(6) of the Evidence Act 1893 and the
-- src:25643 | legal counsel is required as part of the legal counsel’s
-- src:25644 | duties of employment or appointment to provide
-- src:25645 | legal advice or assistance in connection with the
-- src:25646 | application of the law or any form of resolution of
-- src:25647 | legal dispute to any other public agency or agencies,
-- src:25648 | the other public agency or agencies as if the legal
-- src:25649 | counsel is also employed by the other public agency
-- src:25650 | or each of the other public agencies; and
-- src:25652 | (c) an employee or officer of the employer;
@ref s 386AE(2) "employer" (src:25634-25652)
GIVEN `the corporation is related under section 6 to the corporation that employs the legal counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a public agency within the meaning of section 128A(6) of the Evidence Act 1893, the legal counsel is required as part of the legal counsel's duties of employment or appointment to provide legal advice or assistance in connection with the application of the law or any form of resolution of legal dispute to any other public agency or agencies, and the person is that other public agency or one of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee or officer of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AE(2) "employer" the person is within the word employer` MEANS
    IF    `the corporation is related under section 6 to the corporation that employs the legal counsel`
       OR `the employer is a public agency within the meaning of section 128A(6) of the Evidence Act 1893, the legal counsel is required as part of the legal counsel's duties of employment or appointment to provide legal advice or assistance in connection with the application of the law or any form of resolution of legal dispute to any other public agency or agencies, and the person is that other public agency or one of them`
       OR `the person is an employee or officer of the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“employer”, in relation to a legal counsel, includes — (a) ... (b) ... (c) an employee or officer of the employer" leaves the list open

-- src:25654 | “lawyer” means a solicitor or a professional legal adviser, and
-- src:25655 | includes an interpreter or other person who works under the
-- src:25656 | supervision of a solicitor or a professional legal adviser;
@ref s 386AE(2) "lawyer" (src:25654-25656)
GIVEN `the person is a solicitor or a professional legal adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a solicitor or a professional legal adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AE(2) "lawyer" the person is a lawyer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a solicitor or a professional legal adviser` OR `the person is an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a solicitor or a professional legal adviser`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“lawyer” means a solicitor or a professional legal adviser, and includes an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a solicitor or a professional legal adviser" (a "means" definition; the "includes" adds the supervised person: fork line F-AB2)

-- src:25658 | “legal counsel” means a legal counsel as defined in section 3(7)
-- src:25659 | of the Evidence Act 1893, and includes an interpreter or other
-- src:25660 | person who works under the supervision of a legal counsel.
@ref s 386AE(2) "legal counsel" (src:25658-25660)
GIVEN `the person is a legal counsel as defined in section 3(7) of the Evidence Act 1893` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a legal counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AE(2) "legal counsel" the person is a legal counsel` MEANS
    IF `the person is a legal counsel as defined in section 3(7) of the Evidence Act 1893` OR `the person is an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a legal counsel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“legal counsel” means a legal counsel as defined in section 3(7) of the Evidence Act 1893, and includes an interpreter or other person who works under the supervision of a legal counsel" (a "means" definition; the "includes" adds the supervised person: fork line F-AB2)
